>I thought that as of 5.2, or something, VMS did 'true' highwater marking with
>very little overhead. An upgrade of VMS somewhere along the line turned back
>on the highwater marking that I had specifically turned off. What kind of
>overhead does the new highwater marking entail?

I believe, and I could be wrong, that with highwater marking, when the operating 
system is asked for a page of disk memory, it clears the memory prior to giving
it to the asker, with the highwater off, it isn't cleared.  Therefore, if you
are going to be paging only to a disk, and aren't too worried about security,
turning this off should result in less overhead (the clearing of the memory).

Of course I could be wrong, hopefully someone will correct me if I am.

						.dave.

