So I thought about it and experimented until I tried the following. My premise
was that the keymappings would be correct if changed by a child process that
goes away. What I do is execute 

xterm -e telnet.csh

where telnet.csh is

#!/bin/csh
#
# telnet.csh 
#
xmodmap -e "keycode 101 = Delete"
#
xterm -sb -sl 1024 -e telnet vaxhost &
sleep 30   # 30 seconds to login
xmodmap -e "keycode 101 = BackSpace"
exit

This causes me to have a Vax window running as a background process of a child
hp process which goes away in 30 seconds.  This works 95% of the time.
Honestly, the other 5% of the time, the Backspace key reverts to ^H within the
VAX window (which positions the cursor at the BOL). 

Any thoughts about why the behavior is inconsistent? 

No pride issue, if you have a better solution, I'm all ears.

Next up: getting EDT/TPU to work in the VAX window with the correct keypad
keys. If you've done it, please let me know how.

