Marc,

  I forwarded your inquiry off to one of my software counterparts, he sent me
back the following response to your note:

>>i have been trying to figure out how to hook up the 8 serial line
>>TURBOCHANNEL device.  during boot, all of this is printed:

>>real mem = 25165824
>>avail mem = 19972096
>>using 614 buffers containing 2514944 bytes of memory
>>KN02 processor - system rev 32
>>cpu0 ( version 2.0, implementation 2 )
>>fpu0 ( version 3.0, implementation 3 )
>>Module TC400TTY not in tc_option data table, can't configure it

>>[more stuff about drives, etc. follows until boot is done]


>>my basic question is "How do i put TC400TTY in my tc_option data table?"
>>the file "/sys/data/tc_option_data.c" has information about turbo-channel
>>options.



1: Edit /usr/sys/data/tc_option_data.c adding a line describing your device:

  ie. { "OPT_NAME  ",    "xx",     0,      1,    'D',    0},

        Where:  "OPT_NAME " is the 8 character identifier in the option PROM.
                "xx" is the name of your device driver. This allows the
                 TurboChannel auto configuration code to map your option
                 to your device. You can get the option identifier by entering
		
				>>cnfg

		 at the console prompt.

   So his entry would be:

	{ "TC400TTY",    "tcsp",     0,      1,    'D',    0},

   Don't forget to make a new kernel after editing tc_option_data.c.


>>other information:

>>model number on serial port device:  H3104
>>Model:  DECstation 5000/200



