>In article <PRZEMEK.92Sep22160609@rrdstrad.nist.gov>, przemek@rrdstrad.nist.gov (Przemek Klosowski) writes...
>> 
>>I am working on a problem that involves exchanging files between VMS
>>and Ultrix computers.  The data file is fixed record/320 byte on VMS
>>side; I copy it over to Ultrix, massage gently and send back to VMS
>>using binary mode (actually I open pipe to dcp -i if it matters).
>>Unfortunately, the file appears on the VMS side as fixed record/512
>>byte file, which does not do.
>> 
>You can use
>	EXCHANGE/NETWORK u*x::file file
>  from VMS

Actually, to preserve the 320 byte fixed length attribute, you will need to say

	EXCHANGE/NET/FDL=FIX320/TRANSFER=BLOCK unixhost::file file

You can generate the FDL file either by ANALYZE/RMS/FDL on the original file,
or by EDIT/FDL.

One possible version of FIX320.FDL is:
FILE
	ORGANIZATION		sequential
RECORD
	BLOCK_SPAN		yes
	CARRIAGE_CONTROL	none
	FORMAT			fixed
	SIZE			320
