>  Was there ever an 8 plane color option for the VAXstation 2000 ?
> The only ones I've ever seen are 4 plane, but I've heard vague
> talk that a 8 plane version existed.  If such a thing is real, what
> would be involved in converting a 4 plane model to 8 ?
> 
> Thanks,
> Bob Armstrong

The VS2000 uses the same GPX 8 plane color option as the VS3100-3X,4X.
It is the VS40X-PA.  You can usually find one from the used dealers for 
under $1,000.  You will also need a different video cable since the pinout
for the signals on the 15 pin connector are now different.  The proper cable 
is BC19S.  If you want color, you will also need a VR290 or other GPX color
monitor.

If you just want 8 plane gray-scale, you can use the VR260.  If you do this,
just connect the GREEN connector to the VR260, and make sure you put 75 ohm 
terminators on the RED and BLUE, using barrel connectors. 

