> #ifdef VMS
>   event = 3;

=o= This part is pretty important.  Your EFN has to be in the
local event flag cluster.  It can't be one of the ones gotten
with lib$get_ef().

=o= This can be a hassle, especially if you're dealing with some
third-party software (or if you yourself are making third-party
software), because the EFN you choose might be chosen by
somebody else.  Two ways around this:

  o Make a header file defining macros for EFNs for a project --
    or for all projects, if they must work together.

  o Write your own library routine that returns a unique EFN
    from the local cluster.

    <_Jym_>


