and one Quantum105S disk. Its currently configured with 128M of swap, one
32M swap partition on each of the disks. This machine typically has over 70
users logged into it, and, not suprisingly, it's response isnt so hot.
I've got the kernel down to 1.4M, by being fairly ruthless in what gets
stripped out in terms of optional bits. We've been all over the system,
replacing many DEC shipped programs with better/more efficient ones from
either off the net, or written by people here. 

At the moment, we have the system hitting just about every limit there is,
we occasionally (every few days) run out of swap, but the avm is already at
around 23-25M, so I'm not sure if adding more swap will cause more
