Inspect the ribbon cable from the Power Supply to the BackPlane.
These have a nasty habit of 'losing their grip' as they age.
Then, if they develop a critical amount of electrical resistance,
they can overheat and further degrade, sometimes ending in meltdown
of the plastic insulation.  I have seen enough of these wiring harness
fires to know that they are high on the list of hypotheses when
diagnosing general failures.

To inspect the ribbon cable, remove it and look carefully at the
metal pins for signs of carbonization.

Barry Kort


