	For UNIX or VMS? The reason I ask is because UNIX systems (with
reasonable sized caches) tend to be write-bound, while VMS is - well, I
am not sure. ;) Anyhow, It's my strong suspicion that for the cost of
DSSI versus SCSI you could easily buy more RAM for the system (which
will increase general performance) or prestocache (which will increase
some types of filesystem performance in a big way).

1) "Are you sure you're going to be I/O bound?" is the first question.
2) "What O/S are you using?"
3) "Is the bulk of your I/O reads?"
4) "Does your I/O fall in cache-friendly patterns?"
5) "Have you considered IPI?" if #1 above is true.
6) "Have you tried more RAM and increasing cache?" if #4 and #3 are true

