> The VAXELN Window Server software (aka EWS) V1.2 supports the VLC. Basically,
> it turns the VLC into an X Window Terminal and it won't have to page at all. 

You can also improve performance somewhat by removing the machine from the
cluster and running it as a standalone system.  You can run sessions on the
clustered systems by connecting to the via SET HOST and then using the SET
DISPLAY and/or CREATE /TERMINAL commands.  This effectively makes your node
an X terminal, too, but you don't have to go out and buy EWS first.  You
still have local VMS processing power if you want to do things locally, but
you don't have to suffer the cluster overhead and painfully slow bootup.

