>It ought to work.  It certainly works with a VMS box as the host.  This shows
>that there isn't anything in the terminal server that prevents it from working.
>The only concern is therefore for the Ultrix side of things.  
>
it does work, that's about all I can say, both incomming and outgoing 
connections.  I was able to do this from ultrix versions 3.0(3.1??), 4.0, &
4.1.  some notes to consider.

1) if you use a high speed modem, expect very poor transfer speeds.
(i.e. I saw with a telebit T2500 to T2500 approx 900cps which increased
to about 1200 cps when moved directly to a serial port) but 2400
shouldn't be a problem.

2) under ultrix 4.X you need to set a port as such:
	/etc/latcp -h /dev/ttyxx:SERVER:PORT_1 
	(I think that's the right syntax)
you will also need to set the /etc/ttys entry to modem and shared

3) dec wants the modem set up pretty strangly, if I remember correctly
is DCD is high all the time except it winks when Carrier is lost. DSR
follows the carrier on the line.

4) do not use XON/XOFF flow control on the terminal server, if you need
flow control at all, use CTS/RTS, but then again you shouldn't need it
at all with uucp only.

my suggestion in setting up the modem is to:
set up the modem so that DSR is high all the time, and DCD follows 
carrier detect, only disadvantage is that you will have to set up the
L.sys file to do the dialing as part of the chat script (big deal)

now its been a while since I set up a modem for outgoing under ultrix,
but it does work, any more than that, your on your own. :-)


