I just latched on to a Zyxel 1496S with the 5.01 Roms.

The U has a modem pool, with a bunch of prometheus 2400 baud modems, and
a bunch of the DEC scholar? modems.

If I leave the zyxel in multi-auto mode, where it figures out the line
conditions, best speed, etc., it is unable to connect at 2400.  I get
'CONNECT 2400', then a bunch of garbage, then 'NO CARRIER'.

It connects fine at 2400 to other zyxels, and other modems, just has
problems with the above listed ones.

The solution... Tell the modem to not do error detection, nor data 
compression, so that it's a straight 2400 baud connection, and it connects
just fine.

I don't remember the register off the top, but it's on the card that
came with themodem.

Once you take it out of multi-auto mode, it works fine, and makes the
connection just fine.

For what it's worth.
