    In short, you need to use the ACCOUNTING/BINARY/SINCE=/OUTPUT= command.
This will create a new accounting file with only records since the date
you specify. We purge ours about every two to three months. I've made a
small command file to do this, and I submit it to batch when needed. I've 
included a generic copy of the file below. You can edit it to replace the
DEVICE:[DIRECTORY] with your own specifications. You'll probably also
want to edit the line that enables accounting to specify only the types
YOU want accounting to keep track of.

-Howard
================================ CUT HERE ==================================
$!===================================================================+
$! ACCTPURGE.COM                                                     !
$!                                                                   !
$! Command file to shorten the accounting data base to include       !
$! only records since a specified date. The date is passed to the    !
$! procedure with the P1 parameter. If it is omitted, and this is    !
$! being run interactively, the user will be prompted for the        !
$! required date. If it is omitted and this is being run in batch    !
$! mode, the procedure will exit with an error message.              !
$!                                                                   !
$!===================================================================+
$!
$ If ((P1 .EQS. "") .AND. (F$Mode() .EQS. "INTERACTIVE")) Then GoTo Prompt
$ If ((P1 .EQS. "") .AND. (F$Mode() .NES. "INTERACTIVE")) Then GoTo Err_Exit
$Start:
$ Accounting/Binary/OutPut=DEVICE:[DIRECTORY]TempAcc.Dat -
  /Since='P1'
$ Set Accounting/Disable
$ Delete Sys$Manager:Accountng.Dat;*
$ Copy DEVICE:[DIRECTORY]TempAcc.Dat Sys$Manager:Accountng.Dat
$ Delete DEVICE:[DIRECTORY]TempAcc.Dat
$ Set Accounting -
  /Enable=(process,interactive,login,subprocess,detached,batch,network,message)
$ Exit
$Prompt:
$ Inquire/NoPunc P1 "Since Date: "
$ If (P1 .EQS. "") Then GoTo Prompt
$ GoTo Start
$Err_Exit:
$ Write Sys$OutPut "%ACCTPURGE-F-NODATE, Required Since Date missing..."
$ Exit

