   Note: This is a continuum not a toggle.

2) Strong: 1) + Source code is available.

Perhaps a counterexample is in order.  In the past IBM published
an interface called ECF, for building client/servers.  Although the
interface was sufficiently well documented that you could build
clients/servers to those interfaces, because the information/control
flows (over the wire) were not documented, these clients/servers
could not interoperate.  There is no way this could be considered an
open system.


