QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS

Q. Why is Digital starting to manufacture its own PCs?

A. At this point in time Digital has achieved a volume of PC sales worldwide 
   that makes it reasonable for us to manufacture our own PCs.  By doing so 
   we are capable of providing a superior-quality PC at a highly competitive 
   price, which is exactly what customers are looking for.  We see 
   tremendous market opportunity and are vigorously pursuing it.

Q. With so many PCs already available, why would customers choose Digital 
   PCs?

A. We believe that customers want quality, reliability, service, support, 
   and the right price -- all from a stable worldwide supplier.  We can 
   deliver all that and more.

Q. What are some of the tactics we'll be using to achieve our worldwide 
   goals?

A. The underlying strategy is in a new business model designed to make our 
   PC operation more streamlined and efficient.  Digital can increase 
   profitability by taking advantage of the cost efficiencies of controlling 
   all aspects of the product cycle, from concept and design through 
   sourcing of components, final assembly and test, distribution, sales, 
   service and support.   Also, local integration of components in 
   geographies allows shipment of finished product to customers faster as 
   well as making it possible to respond quickly to changes in local market 
   demand.  In the U.S., local integration will be done in Springfield, MA.

Q. How will our relationship with Tandy change with the introduction of 
   these new Digital manufactured desktop PCs?

A. Digital's relationship with Tandy remains strong and will evolve as our 
   business model evolves.  Tandy will no longer manufacture desktop PCs for 
   Digital to sell.  They will, however, continue to manufacture Notebooks 
   and Portables for Digital.

   In addition, Intel will continue to manufacture high-performance systems 
   based on the collaborative design effort between our two companies. 



